    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Counting Hall",
    "overview": "Screening is presented as a public count, not a leaderboard. Every record is accounted for the way ballots are in a counting hall: a strip at the top of every screen states how many records were expected, scored, held for review and failed, and that count must reconcile. White result sheets sit on ruled form stock, a slate rail frames the hall, and one indelible violet ink is reserved for what a person has verified.\n\nThe system is dense, calm and typographic. Chrome is minimal so type, rules and tabular numerals carry structure; a role's result sheet reads like a round-wise result form, criteria as rounds and the total last. Machine assessment and human review are visibly separate layers: the reviewer never edits the machine's marks, and states are stamped and recorded, never hidden. It is a light theme by scene: HR reviewers at a desk under office light, reading tables for long stretches.\n\nIt refuses the grey SaaS dashboard with score donuts and gradient KPI tiles.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ruled 24px slate-blue form stock behind white sheets",
      "Slate shell rail; ink-navy text on paper",
      "Violet only for human marks, focus and selection",
      "Round seal marks: shape plus word, colour only reinforces",
      "One fixed 0–100 score scale with 35/55/75 ticks on every bar",
      "Public Sans with tabular numerals throughout counts and scores",
      "Soft radius tokens (chip 6, control 8, card 12), never pills"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Indelible Ink Rule",
        "body": "Violet marks only what a person has done or is doing: human review marks (In review, Verified, Shortlisted, Not shortlisted), the review submit action, focus, and selection. Machine output is never violet.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shape-Plus-Word Rule",
        "body": "No state is carried by colour alone. Every evidence state is a round seal glyph distinguished by fill (solid, half, empty, dashed) plus its label; where the label is visually dropped it stays in the accessible name.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Count Rule",
        "body": "Every count, rank, score, point value and month figure uses tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Stock Rule",
        "body": "The 24px ruled stock lives behind sheets, on the content field. It never appears inside a table, card or panel; sheets are always solid white.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep violet for human review marks, the review action, focus and selection only.",
      "Do pair every state with a shape and a word; keep the word in the accessible name when it is hidden.",
      "Do put the ruled 24px stock behind sheets and keep sheets solid white.",
      "Do use the chip (6px), control (8px) and card (12px) radius tokens, nested by size.",
